            </profile>
            <profile id="2df6-2887-c681-4b28" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="b792-78e1-7b03-d4d6" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Armed with a hand weapon. May have a Noble Sword (+2 pts), shield (+2), light armour (+2). May ride in a four-horse heavy chariot bought from the Chariotry list (not enforced). If no other Army General is taken, the Marquis may be made Army General for +25 pts. Rightful Conduct (Spring and Autumn period only). 0-1. Designer's note: during the Zhou Dynasty armies would be led at the highest level by a duke representing the state; the King did not indulge in combat. (The Art of War p.29)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="96e2-203f-8636-4b14" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
