  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="613a-1ad3-95b2-83e4" name="Zhou Dynasty (Art of War) - List Notes" publicationId="b792-78e1-7b03-d4d6" hidden="false">
      <description>ZHOU DYNASTY (The Art of War, pp.28-31). Special rules: Heroic Combat (Zhou nobles seek out a worthy opponent; stylised opening duels), Rightful Conduct (Spring and Autumn only: any character with it must accept any Challenge or Heroic Combat offered; must test Leadership to restrain from pursuing a fleeing enemy character or unit containing one; restraining adds bonus VPs, destroying loses them: 3 Wounds 150 VPs, 2 Wounds 100 VPs, 1 Wound 50 VPs). Archers must be added to Spearmen or Halberdiers. Percentage limits are by points. "May only have one selected option per 1,000 points" for Special Units is documented only.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Zhou Dynasty - Western Zhou period]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry: up to 33%
  Infantry: at least 33%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  ZHOU DYNASTY - WESTERN ZHOU PERIOD. Characters up to 25%. Chariotry up to 33%. Infantry at least 33%. Special Units up to 25% (one selected option per 1,000 points). Rightful Conduct and the Duke of Song apply to the Spring and Autumn period only (not enforced).
[Zhou Dynasty - Spring and Autumn period]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry: up to 25%
